A man living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Est.3.1;
son of: Hammedatha (H4099); married to Zeresh (H2238);
father of: Parshandatha (H6577), Dalphon (H1813), Aspatha (H0630), Poratha (H6334), Adalia (H0118), Aridatha (H0743), Parmashta (H6534), Arisai (H0747), Aridai (H0742), Vaizatha (H2055)
§ Haman = "magnificent"
chief minister of Ahasuerus, enemy of Mordecai and the Jews, who plotted to kill the Jews but, being foiled by Esther, was hanged, with his family, on the gallows he had made for Mordecai

A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.8;
son of: Koz (H6976);
brother of: Anub (H6036) and Zobebah (H6637);
father of: Aharhel (H0316)
§ Harum = "exalted"
a man of Judah, father of Aharhel

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.11.26;
son of: Terah (H8646);
brother of: Abraham (H0085), Nahor (H5152H) and Sarah (H8283);
father of: Lot (H3876), Milcah (H4435) and Iscah (H3252)
§ Haran = "mountaineer"
1) youngest son of Terah, brother of Abraham, father of Lot, Milcah, and Iscah; born and died in Ur of the Chaldees
2) a Gershonite Levite in the time of David, one of the family of Shimei
3) a son of Caleb by the concubine Ephah
4) name of the place to which Abraham migrated from Ur of the Chaldees and where the descendants of his brother Nahor established themselves; probably located in Mesopotamia, in Padanaram, the cultivated district at the foot of the hills between the Khabour and the Euphrates below Mount Masius

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Est.9.9;
son of: Haman (H2001);
brother of: Parshandatha (H6577), Dalphon (H1813), Aspatha (H0630), Poratha (H6334), Adalia (H0118), Aridatha (H0743), Parmashta (H6534), Arisai (H0747) and Aridai (H0742)
§ Vajezatha = "strong as the wind"
one of the 10 sons of Haman who were hanged with their father

A man of the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Jos.7.1;
son of: Zerah (H2226I);
brother of: Ethan (H0387H), Heman (H1968H), Calcol (H3633H) and Dara (H1873);
father of: Carmi (H3756H); also called Zimri at 1Ch.2.6;
Also named: <i>zim.ri</i> (זִמְרִי "Zimri" H2174I)
§ Zabdi = "endowment"
1) son of Zerah and grandson of Judah; grandfather of Achan
2) one of the sons of Shimhi, a Benjamite
3) an officer of David, in charge of the produce of the vineyards for the wine-cellars
4) son of Asaph the minstrel; also called 'Zaccur' and 'Zichri'

A man of the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Jos.7.1;
son of: Zerah (H2226I);
brother of: Ethan (H0387H), Heman (H1968H), Calcol (H3633H) and Dara (H1873);
father of: Carmi (H3756H); also called Zimri at 1Ch.2.6;
Another name of <i>zav.di</i> (זַבְדִּי "Zabdi" H2067G)
§ Zimri = "my music"
an obscure name mentioned in connection with 'the mingled people' in Jeremiah; may be same as 'Zimran'

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ki.4.5;
son of: Nathan (H5416H);
brother of: Azariah (H5838H)
§ Zabud = "given"
a priest, son of Nathan, who held the post of 'king's friend' to Solomon

A woman living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ki.23.36;
daughter of: Pedaiah (H6305); married to Josiah (H2977);
mother of: Jehoiakim (H3079)
§ Zebudah = "given"
wife of Josiah and mother of Jehoiakim, both kings of Judah

A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.11.19;
son of: Rehoboam (H7346) and Mahalath (H4258H);
brother of: Jeush (H3266K) and Shemariah (H8114H);
half-brother of: Abijah (H0029I), Attai (H6262I), Ziza (H2124H) and Shelomith (H8019G)
§ Zaham = "loathing"
the son of Rehoboam by Mahalath, David's granddaughter
